From: Venus Build Fix <noreply@example.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Kconfig.venus: select the remaining container-required
 cgroup v2 controllers

The VENUS symbol's cgroups selects only cover CGROUPS, CGROUP_CPUACCT,
CGROUP_SCHED and CFS_BANDWIDTH - enough for the cpu controller, but
nothing for cpuset, memory, io or pids. On boards whose own defconfig
happens to already set these (the rpi family), this is a no-op; on
boards that don't (einstein, am62xx), containers get a cgroup.controllers
of just "cpu" and podman's --memory/--cpuset-cpus/--pids-limit have
nothing to attach to. Select them from Kconfig.venus so the full v2
controller set is consistently available across every machine that can
run containers, rather than depending on per-board defconfig defaults.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Venus specific]

---
 Kconfig.venus | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/Kconfig.venus
+++ b/Kconfig.venus
@@ -45,6 +45,10 @@
 	select CGROUP_CPUACCT
 	select CGROUP_SCHED
 	select CFS_BANDWIDTH
+	select CPUSETS
+	select MEMCG
+	select BLK_CGROUP
+	select CGROUP_PIDS
 
 	# system options
 	select VDSO
